In article <14770@umn-cs.CS.UMN.EDU> clark@umn-cs.CS.UMN.EDU (Robert P. Clark) writes:
>
>  I have a couple questions about NetHack 3.0.  I don't know if these
>are bugs or what, so I'll just ask dumbly.
>
>1) Is it necessary to be able to pick up a chest (bag, sack, whatever else)
>   in order to see what is in it?  You mean I can't look in the bag that I
>   am standing on top of without picking it up?

Try #loot.  This works with bags as well as chests, though it doesn't
say so.  I took the contents of a bag once (a spellbook) when I
couldn't lift the bag this way.

>2) One time I filled a bag with stuff and then dropped it.  I could not pick
>   it up again, even after dropping everything else.  What's up here?

See above.  I think the bag, seemingly a replacement of the
archaeologist's 'large box' is as heavy.  Seems a bit outrageous to me.

>3) I read a scroll of genocide once, but every time I put a letter of a
>   monster to genocide, it told me there was no such monster in the game.
>   I tried several letters, even my feline, but no go.  Was the scroll just
>   cursed or what?

Hm...don't know...have yet to meet a scroll of genocide (have yet to
survive past dlev 4!! :-) )

>4) Why is a homunculus represented by the letter "i"?  Are there any problems
>   with the letters used to represent the monsters - some of the names don't
>   seem to fit the monsters very well.

I believe because a homonculus is considered to be one of many types
of 'imps'.  There are others, I'm sure, but don't know what they are.

Similarly, I believe goblins are 'o's.  Does this mean they're related
to orcs (which are also 'o's)?

Here's a tip...try / to see all the new creatures...your jaw will drop
(there are LICHES, folks!!)  Also, apparantly in an effort to make
NetHack more like moria (though I haven't played the game) there are
differently aged dragons (while halleucinating one time my kitten
turned into a baby green dragon!!)

Anyone get their kitten to grow into a cat yet?  I keep dying first...

NH3.0 is HARD!!! :-)

Nice job, though guys (though I will admit the doors are a bit
annoying...)

